starship --- the prompt thingie. that stuff drawn next to your cursor.

  what    a cross-shell prompt: dir, git branch, status symbols, exit code,
          language versions, etc. -- the line before where you type.
  why     same prompt in bash/zsh/fish, fast, configured in one toml instead
          of a pile of escape codes nobody can read.

where it lives in these dotfiles

  install   nix --- nix/modules/shell/starship.nix
  init      shell pkg --- conf.d/99-interactive.sh runs `starship init`
  config    starship/.config/starship.toml (empty == stock defaults for now)
  docs      https://starship.rs/config/
